# Files excluded from the config context HCP Terraform (Terraform Cloud) uploads
# on CLI-driven runs. The remote workspace roots at infra/environments/ but the
# uploader captures the whole repo, so anything here that isn't Terraform config
# is dead weight — or worse, breaks the upload.
#
# The bazel-* entries are symlinks into the sandbox execroot
# (/private/var/tmp/_bazel_*). Their trees contain build outputs that come and
# go between runs; the uploader follows the symlink and lstat()s files that have
# since been cleaned, failing the run with "no such file or directory". They are
# never Terraform configuration — exclude them.
bazel-bin
bazel-bossanova
bazel-out
bazel-testlogs

# Not Terraform config; large and irrelevant to the uploaded context.
.git
node_modules
